Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 01:10:07 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] test(gateway): isolate four authority tests' relative homes
 in a tmp cwd [daveey]

CI run 44964378873 (attempt 1, sync/upstream head 6e76a5bc8270) failed four
teardowns with "test seeded a Hermes home inside the repo checkout ... a symbolic
profile_id is a relative home, use usefixtures('authority_cwd_in_tmp')":

  tests/gateway/test_discard_delivers_captured_answer.py [False]   -> ['p']
  tests/gateway/test_bot_mailbox_async.py                           -> ['default']
  tests/gateway/test_local_turn_origin_execute_code_gate.py         -> ['default']
  tests/gateway/test_notifier_core_drain.py [give-up]               -> ['default']

Each behaviour assertion had passed; the retry of the failed node alone passed.

Cause (measured, not inferred): these tests bind a SessionAuthority to a symbolic
profile_id ('p', 'default'). That id is a RELATIVE home, and the authority's own
owner-loop tasks keep running under it. A task still alive at teardown (for
example _resolved_unknown -> drain_deferred_rows -> physical_target ->
get_compression_tip -> _read_ctx -> apply_database_pragmas -> load_config_readonly
-> ensure_hermes_home) resolves get_hermes_home() to Path('p') and seeds
<cwd>/p/ with the default SOUL.md. Whether that read lands before teardown is a
scheduling race, which is why the whole file failed once in CI and the node-only
retry passed. On a tree without the checkout guard the same write lands silently,
which is why p/, default/, owned/, fixture/ and target/ sit tracked in the repo.

Fix: usefixtures('authority_cwd_in_tmp') (the existing opt-in fixture), module-wide
for the bot-mailbox, execute-code-gate and notifier files (their sibling tests share
the exposure), on the one parametrized test of the discard file. The
strict checkout-home guard, the delivery-once, receipt re-arm, own-turn gate and
human-bypass assertions are untouched; no retry, wait or guard suppression added.

Proof on the failing sync head 6e76a5bc8270 (whole files, HERMES_TEST_FILE_RETRIES=0,
host oversubscribed with 40-48 concurrent runs, the CI guard installed): the exact CI
message reproduced in 2/100 (discard), 7/80 (bot_mailbox_async), 12/80 (execute-code
gate) and 5/160 (notifier core drain, both [apply] and [give-up]) whole-file runs;
with this change 0/100, 0/80, 0/80 and 0/160. A deterministic control (a pytest
hookwrapper replaying a late config read under each symbolic profile id after the test
body) errors every test of all four files on the sync head and passes them all with
this change. The change cherry-picks onto sync head 6e76a5bc8270 without conflicts.
---
 tests/gateway/test_bot_mailbox_async.py                   | 1 +
 tests/gateway/test_discard_delivers_captured_answer.py    | 1 +
 tests/gateway/test_local_turn_origin_execute_code_gate.py | 2 ++
 tests/gateway/test_notifier_core_drain.py                 | 2 ++
 4 files changed, 6 insertions(+)

